# Adjustfile.a2ml — Drift-tolerance contract for Cliometrics.jl
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Cumulative-drift catchment: tolerance bands + corrective actions.

[metadata]
name = "Cliometrics.jl-adjustfile"
project = "Cliometrics.jl"
schema_version = "1.0"
# Authority: advisory (Yard) — continue-with-warnings; auto_fix where deterministic.
# Run with: adjust check    Fix with: adjust fix
#
# NOTE (2026-06-13): rewritten for Cliometrics.jl. The estate-carried file was the
# rsr-template-repo Adjustfile (drift checks about "template placeholders").

@abstract:
Drift tolerances and corrective actions for Cliometrics.jl. Unlike MUST (hard
gate), ADJUST tracks cumulative drift against tolerance bands and proposes
corrective actions. Advisory — it warns and trends, it does not block.
@end

## Metadata Drift

### state-currency
- description: 6a2/STATE.a2ml last-updated should track real activity
- tolerance: last-updated within ~30 days of the most recent feature commit
- corrective: refresh .machine_readable/6a2/STATE.a2ml (version snapshot + milestones)
- severity: advisory

### version-sync
- description: STATE.a2ml version should match Project.toml version
- tolerance: version fields agree
- corrective: update STATE.a2ml to match Project.toml
- severity: advisory

## Governance Drift

### no-template-identity-leak
- description: contractiles must describe Cliometrics.jl, not rsr-template-repo
- tolerance: 0 contractiles claiming to be the canonical template
- corrective: substitute repo identity; rewrite template-role prose for this repo
- severity: advisory
- notes: the estate flat-contractile set shipped un-substituted (see Mustfile/Intentfile/Adjustfile/Trustfile headers); upstream template fix tracked separately

### contractile-completeness
- description: all six flat contractiles + Justfile present
- tolerance: Adjust/Bust/Dust/Intent/Must/Trust .a2ml + Justfile all exist
- corrective: add the missing contractile
- severity: advisory

## Test Drift

### test-baseline
- description: Julia test suite should not silently regress
- tolerance: all testsets in test/runtests.jl pass (main growth/convergence/institutional/historical suites)
- corrective: investigate dropped/ignored tests before merge
- severity: advisory

### ffi-abi-stability
- description: Zig FFI ABI should not change without a corresponding Julia-side update
- tolerance: ffi/ and src/ ABI surfaces remain consistent
- corrective: review ffi/zig/ and ext/ when either side changes
- severity: advisory

## Hygiene Drift

### spdx-header-consistency
- description: all source files carry an SPDX-License-Identifier
- tolerance: 0 files missing SPDX headers
- corrective: add MPL-2.0 SPDX headers (the estate REUSE sweep covers the bulk)
- severity: advisory

### doc-currency
- description: README.adoc feature list should reflect what is actually implemented
- tolerance: 0 features marked ✅ that are not in src/Cliometrics.jl
- corrective: move un-landed features to planned/v0.3.0 section
- severity: advisory
